  "details": "On the website, a world which has been subject to a copyright takedown notice under DMCA still appears with full details in \"Favorite Worlds\". These worlds can also be moved to different favorite world lists.\n\nIn the Steam client, these worlds appear as \"World Unavailable\" and can only be removed from favorites.\n\nAffected world: [＜＞＜ AVATARS](https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_0d53684b-48b2-48d8-9e68-c49244ccbf61) (`wrld_0d53684b-48b2-48d8-9e68-c49244ccbf61`) by TheZiver - note you can't normally access this world's information in a browser.\n\nIt's unclear to me what the expected behavior is here. Attempting to view the HTML source of the URL above does not leak metadata - such as the picture or world name - from meta tags, and the unavailability of information page in browser suggests to me this is information is meant to be private and not visible in the \"Favorite Worlds\" list.",
